      "source_id": "mod_rules",
      "target_type": "mechanism",
      "target_id": "IMS4-EQ4.26",
      "support_type": "computationally_supported",
      "locator": {
        "page": 66,
        "equation": "4.26"
      },
      "confidence": 0.75,
      "curator_note": "Cross-linked MØD rules. IMS_4_26_1 ([_A]1[C]2([H]3)([H]4)[O+.]5[_A]6 >> [_A.]1.[C]2([H]3)([H]4){=}[O+]5[_A]6) MATCHES step_alpha_cleavage: it cleaves the R'-CH2 bond (incident to the pi-forming carbon), forms the CH2=O(+) double bond and quenches the O radical -- exactly moves 1-3. IMS_4_26_2 ([C]1([H]2)([H]3){=}[O+]4[_A]5 >> [C]1([H]2)([H]3)[O]4.[_A+]5) cleaves the correct O-R bond and yields R(+), matching the connectivity change of step_inductive_cleavage, BUT its product neutral is written with a SINGLE C-O bond ([C]([H])([H])[O]), dropping the C=O double bond of formaldehyde; as written it does not conserve bond order/electrons on the neutral (would give a C/O diradical) rather than neutral CH2=O. Flagged in rule_mismatches."
    }
